=== meta ===
rule: SUBJECT_NORMALIZED
title: A different argument is a different test, not a laundered one
origin: FP guard — argument containment must contain, not merely differ
note: reclassified 2026-09-21 (issue #93 contract decision, estate T-436,
note2: DECISIONS D-060): s and t resolve to different concrete literals
note3: on both sides, so the swap is input laundering, not an unreadable
note4: replacement — SUBJECT_INPUT_CHANGED fires. SUBJECT_NORMALIZED
note5: correctly stays silent: nothing wraps the old subject.
=== before: tests/test_encode.py ===
from app import encode_path


def test_non_ascii():
    s = "caf\u00e9"
    t = "na\u00efve"
    assert encode_path(s) == "caf%C3%A9"
=== after: tests/test_encode.py ===
from app import encode_path


def test_non_ascii():
    s = "caf\u00e9"
    t = "na\u00efve"
    assert encode_path(t) == "caf%C3%A9"
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "SUBJECT_INPUT_CHANGED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["NO_PROD_CHANGE_IN_DIFF"]}]
